From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Give SP and DP edges priority, reserve queue slots, carry the source

The scheduler's interrupt queue holds eight messages and serves three things at
once: our retrace edges, our SP and DP edges, and -- through the command queue
that __scHandleRetrace drains -- the game's own task submissions. One retrace too
many takes the place of a task completion, and of a task start.

Measured on Windows 95: the RSP completion was refused, requeued, and deposited
only nine refusals later. The game does not wait that long; a few frames without
an answer and its scheduler gives up and clears curRSPTask. Our message then
arrives and __scHandleRSP dereferences null, the assert() that would have caught
it having been compiled out.

**Priority.** On hardware an SP interrupt and a vertical retrace are independent
events whose relative order is not guaranteed, so serving SP and DP first is
faithful. Their order among themselves is preserved.

**Reserved slots.** A first attempt refused to deposit a retrace while the
previous one was undelivered. It stopped the game booting: our external queue is
drained opportunistically, when a guest thread happens to wait, not on a
schedule, so the flag stayed set. Any policy assuming periodic draining is wrong
here by construction. This version reads the guest queue's state at deposit time
and keeps nothing between passes -- on hardware a retrace raised while the queue
is full is lost the same way.

**The source travels with the message.** enqueue_external_message_src did not
record it, so everything passing through carried the default. Both policies above
then missed their target: the priority promoted only SP, the one edge that goes
through the waiting variant, and the reservation meant for retraces could discard
a DP edge, which looked identical to it.

That defect did not show in the counts -- nothing was refused, so nothing seemed
missing. It showed because a probe conditioned on the source never fired while
544 DP messages were being deposited.

Measured before and after the whole change:

    before   1 task, 1 SP edge, 0 display lists
    after   555 display lists, 3720 frames, no message refused, and
            curRDPTask non-null at every one of 500 DP deposits

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
--- a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
@@ -142,7 +142,18 @@
     if (mq == NULLPTR) {
         return;
     }
-    external_messages.enqueue({mq, msg, jam, requeue_enabled[static_cast<int>(src)], {}});
+    // **The source must travel with the message.**
+    //
+    // Without it, everything that passes through here carries the default value,
+    // and two policies written just above miss their target: the priority given
+    // to the SP and DP edges promotes only SP - the only one to go through the
+    // expected variant - and the slot reservation meant for the retraces can
+    // discard a DP edge, which then looks like its twin.
+    //
+    // The defect did not show in the counts: nothing was refused, so nothing
+    // seemed to be missing. It showed because a probe conditioned on the source
+    // never fired, while 544 DP messages were being deposited.
+    external_messages.enqueue({mq, msg, jam, requeue_enabled[static_cast<int>(src)], {}, src});
 }
 
 bool ultramodern::enqueue_external_message_src_and_wait(PTR(OSMesgQueue) mq, OSMesg msg, bool jam, EventMessageSource src) {
@@ -236,6 +247,34 @@
                 continue;
             }
         }
+        // **Read the game's state at deposit time, not afterwards.**
+        //
+        // The remaining crash finds `curRDPTask` null in `__scHandleRDP`. Two
+        // causes remain and can only be told apart there: either we emit a DP
+        // edge for a task the game has not registered as needing the RDP - it
+        // would then already be null when we deposit - or the game clears it
+        // between our deposit and its handling.
+        //
+        // The address is that of `gMainSched` in DKR, taken from the decomp's
+        // symbol map. Hard-coding it would not be acceptable elsewhere; here it
+        // is a diagnostic behind an environment variable, and the only way to
+        // ask the question.
+        if (to_send.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Dp &&
+            std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP") != nullptr) {
+            static unsigned nulls = 0, set = 0, shown = 0;
+            /* The guest RDRAM is stored byte-swapped on the host side: we read
+               the word backwards to recover the game's value. */
+            const uint8_t* o = rdram + (0x801214D8u - 0x80000000u);
+            const uint32_t cur = (uint32_t)o[3] | ((uint32_t)o[2] << 8) |
+                                 ((uint32_t)o[1] << 16) | ((uint32_t)o[0] << 24);
+            if (cur == 0u) { nulls++; } else { set++; }
+            if (++shown <= 6u || (nulls + set) % 100u == 0u) {
+                std::fprintf(stderr,
+                             "[trace][dp] curRDPTask at deposit = 0x%08X"
+                             "  (nulls=%u set=%u)\n",
+                             (unsigned)cur, nulls, set);
+            }
+        }
         const bool sent = do_send(PASS_RDRAM to_send.mq, to_send.mesg, to_send.jam, false);
         // **Count the deposits, not the requests.**
         //
